# Store and check out every file byte-for-byte.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings
# on checkout. This project ships its working copy verbatim — tools/make-release
# zips the files as they sit on disk — so a clone that differs from what was
# tested is a clone nobody tested. `-text` turns EOL conversion off entirely.
#
# It also keeps the mixed endings already here honest: server/serve.js and
# app/js/play.js are CRLF, app/js/hexmap.js and tools/ are LF. Nothing depends
# on that, but silently rewriting 400 files on every clone would bury real
# changes in noise.
* -text
